From student protests across France over the weekend and presidential elections in Brazil pitting leftist incumbent Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva against right-wing challenger Flavio Bolsonaro to wildfires in Indonesia, FRANCE 24 looks back at some of the most striking images from the past week.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd897c30-d056-11f1-8d7f-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-24T194218Z-1784067987-RC2R9OAGSDD5-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-PROTEST.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd897c30-d056-11f1-8d7f-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-24T194218Z-1784067987-RC2R9OAGSDD5-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-PROTEST.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">45987e7e-d05c-11f1-bf57-2d98d87a5fdd</guid><pubDate>Sun, 25 Oct 2026 12:48:31 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd897c30-d056-11f1-8d7f-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-24T194218Z-1784067987-RC2R9OAGSDD5-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-PROTEST.jpg">© Abdul Saboor, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Voting under way across Brazil in tight presidential run-off between Lula and Bolsonaro</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261025-live-voting-under-way-across-brazil-in-tight-presidential-run-off-between-lula-and-bolsonaro</link><description>
Brazil’s 158 million voters decide between leftist President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva and right-wing challenger Senator Flavio Bolsonaro – the son of former president and Trump ally Jair Bolsonaro – following a highly charged run-off campaign period, with the candidates in a dead heat in polls. Follow our liveblog for the latest developments.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4c3d5810-d06d-11f1-987e-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/Brazil-vote.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4c3d5810-d06d-11f1-987e-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/Brazil-vote.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">635aedf6-ced7-11f1-9289-95da0497d4a3</guid><pubDate>Sun, 25 Oct 2026 12:46:02 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4c3d5810-d06d-11f1-987e-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/Brazil-vote.jpg">© Adriano Machado, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Polls open in Brazil presidential runoff</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/polls-open-in-brazil-presidential-runoff</link><description>
Brazilian President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva and sight-wing senator Flavio Bolsonaro faced off Friday in their second and final debate ahead of Sunday's presidential runoff election. The two candidates repeated their campaign proposals, focusing on the cost of living and security, while exchanging ⁠allegations of corruption. France 24 Jan Onoszko telles us the latest from Rio de Janeiro.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f689cca0-d067-11f1-911d-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261025-120157-120549-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f689cca0-d067-11f1-911d-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261025-120157-120549-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fbd61f10-d067-11f1-8c27-3df80effe4d1</guid><pubDate>Sun, 25 Oct 2026 11:40:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Far-right leader Le Pen says visible policing keeps protests smooth</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/far-right-leader-le-pen-says-visible-policing-keeps-protests-smooth</link><description>
Meanwhile, France’s far-right National Rally is holding the second day of its party congress in Orléans, south of Paris. Marine Le Pen is expected to officially launch her presidential campaign in a speech later this afternoon, while Jordan Bardella is being re-elected as party leader. On Saturday, a large counter-demonstration against the far right was held in the city. Our reporter Antonia Kerrigan has been following the latest developments.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5160b9a4-d068-11f1-b673-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261025-121058-121405-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5160b9a4-d068-11f1-b673-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261025-121058-121405-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">56cbc668-d068-11f1-a57b-25b3852b0c3f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 25 Oct 2026 11:39:18 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel: Demonstrators rally against government ahead of election</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israel-demonstrators-rally-against-government-ahead-of-election</link><description>
In Israel, the anti-Netanyahu movement is mobilising. Thousands gathered in Tel Aviv on Friday to protest against the Israeli government, just three days ahead of a general election widely seen as a referendum on Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4abc8a7a-d067-11f1-a9cf-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261025-110931-111122-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4abc8a7a-d067-11f1-a9cf-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261025-110931-111122-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4fa70b32-d067-11f1-84c1-4f61f4eb9a12</guid><pubDate>Sun, 25 Oct 2026 11:38:01 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Obama hits campaign trail for democrats</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/obama-hits-campaign-trail-for-democrats</link><description>
With less than two weeks to go before the US midterm elections, former President Barack Obama has hit the campaign trail, rallying support for Democratic candidates in the key states of Michigan and Ohio. He criticised the Trump administration, blaming the White House for rising living costs, a major concern for voters. Democrats are hoping to regain control of Congress, with polls showing several closely contested races. Ophelie Jacobson has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a6c5f842-d067-11f1-838f-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261025-111149-111339-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a6c5f842-d067-11f1-838f-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261025-111149-111339-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ac035e62-d067-11f1-bea8-35f7b887b3db</guid><pubDate>Sun, 25 Oct 2026 11:36:56 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>West Bank: Families forcibly displaced in Hebron</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/west-bank-families-forcibly-displaced-in-hebron</link><description>
More Palestinian families have been displaced in the occupied West Bank as Israeli forces continue operations in Hebron, following a deadly shooting that killed two Israeli soldiers on Friday. With elections scheduled for Tuesday, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu has vowed a heavy response to the attack. Morgaene Ayre has the latest.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/11d151aa-d067-11f1-9d2a-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261025-110725-110909-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/11d151aa-d067-11f1-9d2a-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261025-110725-110909-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">16e4f84a-d067-11f1-bf8e-31e55578324b</guid><pubDate>Sun, 25 Oct 2026 11:35:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>At least 1,300 people arrested in mass weekend protests across France</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261025-at-least-1-300-people-arrested-in-mass-weekend-protests-across-france</link><description>
At least 1,300 people were arrested on the sidelines of Saturday's protests across France and at least 50 officers and three protesters were hurt, the interior ministry said Sunday. The arrests occurred as clashes broke out on the margins of largely calm demonstrations in major cities over the high cost of living.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b7dd62bc-d05a-11f1-88d3-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26297559777844.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b7dd62bc-d05a-11f1-88d3-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26297559777844.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1061870a-d061-11f1-a8d9-274107ab047a</guid><pubDate>Sun, 25 Oct 2026 11:02:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b7dd62bc-d05a-11f1-88d3-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26297559777844.jpg">© Jean-Francois Badias, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Suspect in racist gun attack near Paris transferred to psychiatric unit</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261025-suspect-in-racist-gun-attack-near-paris-transferred-to-psychiatric-unit</link><description>
A shooter suspected of killing one person and wounding five others on Friday in the town of Trappes, near Paris, has had his police custody suspended for a 48-hour psychiatric observation, anti-terror prosecutors said Sunday. The 39-year-old man is believed to have had racist motivations behind the gun attack as most of the victims had foreign origins.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a69c99f4-d05b-11f1-b633-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D47R7WB.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a69c99f4-d05b-11f1-b633-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D47R7WB.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">01ee3626-d05e-11f1-a0cf-9b2783ed58d1</guid><pubDate>Sun, 25 Oct 2026 10:36:42 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a69c99f4-d05b-11f1-b633-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D47R7WB.jpg">© Dimitar Dilkoff, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France: Some clashes erupted at end of protests</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france-some-clashes-erupted-at-end-of-protests</link><description>
There were some clashes on Saturday, mainly in major cities and as demonstrations came to an end. French authorities say police made nearly 1,000 arrests nationwide. Here’s a report from our sister channel, France 2.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/913459ee-d056-11f1-8548-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261025-090423-090631-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/913459ee-d056-11f1-8548-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261025-090423-090631-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">96ec49f0-d056-11f1-91a9-9db82fb1c219</guid><pubDate>Sun, 25 Oct 2026 09:35:20 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>More than 400.000 protest across France</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/more-than-400-000-protest-across-france</link><description>
Saturday’s demonstrations across France were largely peaceful, easing fears of a repeat of the violence seen last weekend. Hundreds of thousands took to the streets to demand action on the rising cost of living and more funding for public services, with students, workers and retirees marching side by side. Many say their anger shows no sign of fading. The government put turnout at 410,000 nationwide, while the CGT union estimated the figure was almost twice as high. Here’s Jack Pownall with more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4fb7d9d2-d056-11f1-905d-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261025-090147-090407-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4fb7d9d2-d056-11f1-905d-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261025-090147-090407-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">54b08f1a-d056-11f1-b07c-81e176334a8f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 25 Oct 2026 09:32:21 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France’s far right gathers as Le Pen prepares her presidential campaign</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france-s-far-right-gathers-as-le-pen-prepares-her-presidential-campaign</link><description>
Meanwhile, France’s far-right National Rally is holding the second day of its party congress in Orléans, south of Paris. Marine Le Pen is expected to officially launch her presidential campaign in a speech later this afternoon, while Jordan Bardella is being re-elected as party leader. On Saturday, a large counter-demonstration against the far right was held in the city. For more on what’s happening there, let’s cross to our reporter, Antonia Kerrigan.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4f38fff0-d055-11f1-a349-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261025-100832-101312-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4f38fff0-d055-11f1-a349-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261025-100832-101312-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">54b8bb14-d055-11f1-93d0-910454473283</guid><pubDate>Sun, 25 Oct 2026 09:31:02 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Hundreds of thousands march in France to protest against government</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/hundreds-of-thousands-march-in-france-to-protest-against-government</link><description>
Hundreds of thousands marched across France on Saturday protesting the rising cost of living and a lack of government resources for essential services like schools. While demonstrations in Paris started peacefully they ended with a heavy security response, with almost 1,000 arrested across the country. France 24 International Affairs Editor Oliver Farry shares further details.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1c1540d4-d055-11f1-ad06-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261025-100212-100803-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1c1540d4-d055-11f1-ad06-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261025-100212-100803-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">212df264-d055-11f1-8954-1f5a35e6fa2e</guid><pubDate>Sun, 25 Oct 2026 09:29:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Serbia holds parliamentary election as populist leader Vucic faces student movement</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261025-serbia-holds-parliamentary-election-as-populist-leader-vucic-faces-student-movement</link><description>
Serbia votes on Sunday in what is set to be its most contested parliamentary election in more than 14 years, as a student-led movement seeks to oust the party of populist leader Aleksandar Vucic. The vote comes after nearly two years of student-led protests sparked by the 2024 collapse of a canopy that killed 16 people.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d4dc69a-d03c-11f1-a767-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26298218958918.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d4dc69a-d03c-11f1-a767-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26298218958918.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c4d9079e-d043-11f1-8021-2b425011c9ce</guid><pubDate>Sun, 25 Oct 2026 07:14:50 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d4dc69a-d03c-11f1-a767-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26298218958918.jpg">© Petr David Josek, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>What to know as Brazilians choose between Lula and Bolsonaro in tense presidential runoff</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261025-what-to-know-as-brazilians-choose-between-lula-and-bolsonaro-in-tense-presidential-runoff</link><description>
Brazilians are set on Sunday to choose between leftist incumbent President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and far-right candidate Flavio Bolsonaro in the runoff vote of a deeply polarizing presidential election, and one which will determine whether the US significantly expands its growing influence in Latin America.
