The Palestinian Authority has called for international pressure on Israel after a Palestinian official said around 1,200 Palestinians in Hebron in the West Bank were forced to leave their homes following an attack on Friday which killed two Israeli soldiers. The head of Hebron's municipality said an additional 1,300 may also be forced to leave.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c6d1d9fc-cfbe-11f1-b89b-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261024-161247-161339-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c6d1d9fc-cfbe-11f1-b89b-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261024-161247-161339-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cc10e1c4-cfbe-11f1-bc2f-d5fd7e8fb465</guid><pubDate>Sat, 24 Oct 2026 17:13:56 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Italy hit by new cost of living protests</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/italy-hit-by-new-cost-of-living-protests</link><description>
Soldiers were deployed across Milan and luxury boutiques boarded up as protesters took to the streets again on Saturday, a week after looting and clashes with police. Prime Minister Giorgia Meloni announced a series of measures, including sending an additional 500 soldiers to the city and introducing tougher penalties for minors, who police said made up a large proportion of last week’s violent protesters. Surveillance helicopters circled central Piazza del Duomo, while soldiers patrolled in groups alongside military vehicles and a water cannon. Some visitors said they would leave the city centre if violence broke out again. Our Rome correspondent, Seema Gupta, has the latest.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5cb75c7c-cfcd-11f1-9bf9-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261024-171053-171328-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5cb75c7c-cfcd-11f1-9bf9-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261024-171053-171328-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">62097e30-cfcd-11f1-a054-5d9d5970f3ee</guid><pubDate>Sat, 24 Oct 2026 17:12:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Paris: 70.000 police officers deployed nationwide</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/paris-70-000-police-officers-deployed-nationwide</link><description>
A coalition of the “Yellow Vests” movement, trade unions and students will march across France on Saturday with demands over studying conditions and purchasing power. Some 70,000 police are expected to be deployed as authorities fear looting and vandalism similar to last Saturday's unrest. Jennie Shin speaks to France 24's reporter Elitsa Gadeva.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f782198c-cfbd-11f1-8ac9-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261024-160222-160523-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f782198c-cfbd-11f1-8ac9-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261024-160222-160523-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fd1c09ac-cfbd-11f1-bffa-87984c49c255</guid><pubDate>Sat, 24 Oct 2026 17:11:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
